    <summary>High-performance Rust implementation of BitNet 1-bit LLM inference</summary>
    <description>
bitnet-rs is a pre-alpha implementation of BitNet 1-bit Large Language Model inference engine, written in Rust for memory safety and SIMD-optimised CPU inference.

## Features

- **Memory Safety**: Rust's ownership system prevents memory leaks and buffer overflows
- **High Performance**: Zero-cost abstractions and SIMD optimizations
- **Cross-platform**: Native support for Windows, Linux, and macOS
- **Reliability**: Comprehensive error handling and graceful degradation
- **GPU Support**: CUDA acceleration (alpha, not validated)
- **Multiple Interfaces**: CLI, HTTP server, and library APIs

## Included Tools

- **bitnet-cli**: Command-line interface for model inference
- **bitnet-server**: HTTP server for inference API

## Quick Start

After installation, you can use bitnet-rs immediately:

```
# Check version
bitnet-cli --version

# Run inference
bitnet-cli infer --model path/to/model.gguf --prompt "Hello, world!"

# Start server
bitnet-server --port 8080 --model path/to/model.gguf
```

## Documentation

- API Documentation: https://docs.rs/bitnet
- User Guide: https://github.com/EffortlessMetrics/BitNet-rs/blob/main/docs/
- Installation Guide: https://github.com/EffortlessMetrics/BitNet-rs/blob/main/INSTALLATION.md

## Support

- GitHub Issues: https://github.com/EffortlessMetrics/BitNet-rs/issues
- Discussions: https://github.com/EffortlessMetrics/BitNet-rs/discussions
    </description>
